/**
 * PostHog web analytics, for the live site only.
 *
 * The account is Ryan's own PostHog organisation "RC", on US Cloud.
 * The token below is a project token, which PostHog designs to sit in public
 * page source: it can send events and nothing else. It is not a secret, so it
 * is fine in this public repository.
 *
 * ONLY ON jinhyuk.org. This layout is drawn by three things: the GitHub Pages
 * build, the editor on Vercel (its preview frame renders real site pages
 * through Base.astro), and `npm run dev`. The check is on the hostname at run
 * time rather than on a build flag, so the editor, its preview, a local dev
 * server and `astro preview` all stay out of the numbers without any of them
 * having to remember to opt out. www.jinhyuk.org is not listed because GitHub
 * Pages redirects it to the apex before a page loads.
 *
 * The loader is PostHog's own web snippet, verbatim
 * (https://posthog.com/docs/libraries/js). It only queues calls and fetches
 * the real library asynchronously, so it never holds up the first paint.
 * `is:inline` stops Astro bundling it, which would otherwise fail the type
 * check on `window.posthog`.
 *
 * `defaults` pins PostHog's behaviour to that date's settings, so an update
 * on their side cannot quietly change what is collected. It includes
 * pageview capture and $pageleave, which is what the Web analytics dashboard
 * reads.
 */
---

